From 5f23461b2b8eac171f0ba3b9033df10e759b725d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 02:29:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban sync: back off failed rounds; one host card
 for a host-wide Board outage

Incident 2026-11-15 13:25-13:50 PST on laptop-1 (t_example): DNS resolution of the Board failed
(URLError [Errno 8] nodename nor servname provided) on every synced board.

Retry storm: wait_for_work ends its 0.5 s tick whenever a synced outbox has a pending row, push() keeps rows
pending on a transport failure (correct), and SyncWork.select picked any board with pending rows even if its
last round failed, so the loop retried every board about every 0.6 s. The feed socket's 1->60 s backoff never
covered rounds. Now SyncWork backs a failed board off 1 s doubling to 60 s across every leg (pending outbox,
dirty flag, poll, full recovery, deferred repairs, backlog); its pending outbox no longer ends the wait; a
success or its feed socket reconnecting clears the backoff. Pending writes stay queued; healthy boards are
unaffected.

Alert fanout: kanban_sync_replica_age judged each board alone, so one cause filed ten cards. Round failures
are now classified from the exception object (socket.gaierror -> dns; refused/reset/unreachable/timeout ->
network; anything else unclassified). Boards that come due in one check with a classified cause from a recent
round share one host card listing every board and its frozen cards; later boards are added by comment; the
incident (persisted per boot) ends when all members recover and recurrence opens a fresh one. Unclassified
causes and boards with no recent round keep their own per-board card on the same 20-awake-min bound.
Archived boards (board.json archived: true) are no longer judged.

Does not diagnose or change the host's DNS configuration.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_sync_host_outage.py (21) drive sync_all_once/run_forever against an
in-memory Board with injected DNS/503 transport failures and the real Hub with getaddrinfo failing; 12 fail
on origin/main (ten cards, 200 retries per 100 s). Adjacent kanban sync suite: 1625 passed.
